			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"width": 2143.025146484375,
			"height": 1663.2000000000003,
			"seed": 706178337,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"roundness": null,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1747067404642,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"fontSize": 28,
			"fontFamily": 6,
			"text": "Optimisations deep-dive.\n\nPerformance - thousands of tickets and hundreds of columns. we can use pagination together with react-window to render only what's seen and not all of the data. \n\nRendering - lazy load non-critical resources,  for examples modal for adding new column and new ticket, this reduces bundle size and improves rendering on critical\npath.\n\nMight be worth using React.memo for pure UI components like tickets.\n\n\n\nAccessibiltiy - Use semantic HTML instead of divs. We also want to use ARIA attributes so screen reader can have more context what the controls and components are\nfor. Perhaps also allow keyboard navigations.\n\nMonitoring - We can use tools like Datadog to track user events. Such as how many times they click on the add ticket button. It can also be used to track rendering\nperformance and logging.\n\n\nAuthentication - jwt session token in cookie. Every request to server will have cookie to verify user.\n\n\nSSR - if we have a view mode for users less likely to interact with board and static componenets, consider server side rendering to improve performance.\n\n\nNetwork connectivity - have some sort of retry policies.\n\n\nReal-time collaboration - use WebSocket, it's more resource intensive on both client and server due to long living connection unlike HTTP.  When user initiate an action,\nFE emits a WebSocket event which is propagated to all clients.\n\nConflict - resolution - If you update a ticket, we update UI optimistically, and also send request to backend. \nWe can have versioning - eg. timestamp or latest update wins to address conflicts.\n\n\n\nResilience - Per component Error Boundary, eg. a ticket could fail to render due to some bug. Or a column could fail to render due to some bug. We want other parts to\nbe operational.\n\nretry logic when fetching\n\noptimistic update\n\n\n",
			"rawText": "",
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Optimisations deep-dive.\n\nPerformance - thousands of tickets and hundreds of columns. we can use pagination together with react-window to render only what's seen and not all of the data. \n\nRendering - lazy load non-critical resources,  for examples modal for adding new column and new ticket, this reduces bundle size and improves rendering on critical\npath.\n\nMight be worth using React.memo for pure UI components like tickets.\n\n\n\nAccessibiltiy - Use semantic HTML instead of divs. We also want to use ARIA attributes so screen reader can have more context what the controls and components are\nfor. Perhaps also allow keyboard navigations.\n\nMonitoring - We can use tools like Datadog to track user events. Such as how many times they click on the add ticket button. It can also be used to track rendering\nperformance and logging.\n\n\nAuthentication - jwt session token in cookie. Every request to server will have cookie to verify user.\n\n\nSSR - if we have a view mode for users less likely to interact with board and static componenets, consider server side rendering to improve performance.\n\n\nNetwork connectivity - have some sort of retry policies.\n\n\nReal-time collaboration - use WebSocket, it's more resource intensive on both client and server due to long living connection unlike HTTP.  When user initiate an action,\nFE emits a WebSocket event which is propagated to all clients.\n\nConflict - resolution - If you update a ticket, we update UI optimistically, and also send request to backend. \nWe can have versioning - eg. timestamp or latest update wins to address conflicts.\n\n\n\nResilience - Per component Error Boundary, eg. a ticket could fail to render due to some bug. Or a column could fail to render due to some bug. We want other parts to\nbe operational.\n\nretry logic when fetching\n\noptimistic update\n\n\n",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.35
		},
